From 6f0158a08cd763eac4bbc2a830ea52fe27996a87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Zhou <alex.zhou@edge0.ai>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:54:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] moe_pool: android demand-pool phase-1 (copy-in private
 frames + lazy row-ptr + expert LRU)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- ggml-cpu/moe_pool.{c,h}: E0_POOL_MB gate (off by default = zero disturbance); copy-in private
  frames (Android mlock RLIMIT=64KB rules out the pin-file-page design -- PROBE B-track closed);
  demand miss = thread0 bulk pread before the barrier ("wholesale"); eviction = self-managed LRU
  at whole-expert granularity + current-generation protection (rows still in compute are not
  recycled); non-resident row pointers resolve lazily back to the original mmap (kernel backstop).
- ggml-cpu.c MUL_MAT_ID, four hooks: include / IQP bypass disabled (self-computed row pointers
  would skip the pool) / thread0 dispatches ensure after scanning ids / src0_cur row-pointer resolve
- llama-model.cpp load-time registration: walk ml.contexts + name contains 'exps' + weight.offs
  taken directly (stride%4096 conservative gate; pread does not move the file cursor; pointer idempotent)
- Android path gates: llama-model.cpp AUTO mmap_support downgrade skippable (E0_MMAP_NOPREFETCH) +
  bench E0_NO_REPACK + main.cpp setvbuf (root cause of the 217B truncation misattribution)
- concurrency protocol = phase-1 single ctx (node barriers keep readers quiescent while ensure
  writes); server parallel ctx = phase 2

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
